+## Encryption
+
+You can require TLS encryption for the connection to your SQL Server database. When enabled, PostHog refuses to connect if the server does not offer encryption. When disabled (the default), PostHog encrypts only when the server offers it.
+
+To enable encryption, set **Require encryption?** to **Yes** during source setup or on the source's **Configuration** tab.
+
+> **Note:** PostHog does not verify the SQL Server certificate. The driver's certificate authority setting is process-wide, so per-connection verification is not supported. If you need verified TLS, terminate TLS at a proxy or use an SSH tunnel.
+
