+### TLS certificate verification failed
+
+This error occurs when PostHog could not verify your database's TLS certificate. The error message tells you what went wrong:
+
+- **"PostHog could not verify your database's TLS certificate"** — The certificate was not signed by an authority PostHog trusts, or it does not match the host. Add the certificate authority that signed it, check the host, or turn off certificate verification and remove the certificate authority.
+- **"Your database's TLS certificate does not match the host"** — The certificate's hostname does not match the host you entered. Use the hostname the certificate was issued for, or turn off certificate verification and remove the certificate authority.
+- **"Your database rejected the client certificate"** — Your database rejected the client certificate PostHog presented, or it requires one. Add a client certificate and key that your database trusts.
+
 > **Looking for an example of the Postgres source?** Check out our tutorial where we [connect and query Supabase data](/tutorials/supabase-query).
